# Lesson components and practice

When writing or extending lecture MDX, **reuse existing widgets** before inventing new ones. Also follow `lazy-simulators.mdc`, `lesson-activities.mdc`, and `lesson-figures.mdc`.

## Prefer reuse

Globally registered (no MDX import): `MultipleChoice`, `CodeExercise` / `CodingExam`, `ExerciseSet` / `Exercise`, `SqlExercise`, `LessonFigure`, and any `*Simulator` in `lazySimulators.js`.

- Search `src/components/interactive/` and nearby lessons for a simulator or exercise pattern that already fits before adding a new component.
- New heavy interactives: create under `src/components/interactive/`, register in `lazySimulators.js`, use as `<Name />` in MDX — never `import` them in the lesson file.
- Prefer `CodeExercise` for runnable practice; `SqlExercise` for SQL; `MultipleChoice` for concept checks.

## Group multiple questions as sets

If a section has **two or more** coding / practice items (or several related quiz blocks you want as one unit of work), wrap them in `<ExerciseSet>` so they share the tabbed set UI:

```mdx
### Practice: topic

<ExerciseSet>
  <CodeExercise title="First" heading="exercise-first" ... />
  <CodeExercise title="Second" heading="exercise-second" ... />
</ExerciseSet>
```

- Give each child a distinct `title` (and `heading` / `anchor` when used).
- One standalone exercise may stay outside a set; do not invent a set for a single item unless the section will grow.

## Quizzes: shuffle answers

`MultipleChoice` display-shuffles choices, but **authored `answer` indices must still vary** — do not leave almost every question as `answer: 1` (the long option in slot B).

When adding or editing quiz questions:

1. Put the correct choice at a **varied** index (`0`–`3`), not always the second option.
2. Write **wrong options as full parallel explanations** of similar length — not one long correct sentence and three short dismissals.
3. Do not bolt shared filler suffixes onto distractors (no repeated “which stops after…”, “treat it as a misconception…”, etc.).
4. After bulk quiz edits, re-run the matching shuffle script so answer positions stay evenly spread:
   - `fundamentals/scalable-systems/` → `python scripts/fix-scalable-quiz-bias.py`
   - `fundamentals/computer-engineering/` (OS / OSTEP) → `python scripts/fix-os-quiz-bias.py`

```js
// ❌ BAD — always B, longest tells the answer
choices: ['Short wrong', 'Very long correct explanation…', 'Short', 'Short'],
answer: 1,

// ✅ GOOD — varied index, parallel length
choices: [
  'Wrong but complete alternative mechanism…',
  'Another full wrong account of similar length…',
  'The actual correct explanation of similar length…',
  'A third plausible wrong explanation…',
],
answer: 2,
```
